{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1062287-newbie-looking-to-join-run-pbp-game","id":1062287,"title":"Newbie Looking to Join/Run PBP Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-14T07:31:50-07:00","id":1062287,"title":"Newbie Looking to Join/Run PBP Game","content":"Hi!<br /> My name's Mitsu and I love RPGs. I've always wanted to play WoD games but just never had the chance. Now, with the PDFs available for really decent prices and the magic of play-by-post games to work with my busy schedule, I figure I've got a perfect chance.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd love to join in on a new PBP game (I'm hesitant to jump in on an existing one since I figure it's going to be hard enough for a newbie like me to pick things up anyway so learning the whole background of a running game would just add to that) or possibly run one.<br /> <br /> <br /> I know STs are harder to find than players so I don't mind playing that role as long as my players understand that I'm a total newbie and will probably mangle the lore in my ignorance. <br /> <br /> <br /> The game I've run the most is Golden Sky Stories so I'm used to games that are more about emotions than conflict. Also I guess I'm used to my stories being cute? Side effect of the system, I guess. Don't worry, I also love horror so I'm sure I can come up with a good mix of adorable creepy.<br /> <br /> <br /> I haven't played any WoD system so I'm interested in trying pretty much anything, though my priorities are:<br /> Very Interested:<br /> Changeling<br /> Werewolf<br /> <br /> <br /> Interested:<br /> Everything not in the other two lists <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd have to be talked into it:<br /> Mage<br /> Vampire <br /> Beast<br /> Exalted <br /> <br /> <br /> Old? New? 2e? Whatever! I just would like to stick with core books if possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah I'll play your PBP! Though I figure as soon as I wrote 'I'll ST' I sealed my fate. As long as folks are cool with a newb ST (though not new to running RPGs) and can agree on a system I'm very much down to run a game right here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let me know!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13120-matatabimitsu","name":"MatatabiMitsu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:51:04-07:00","id":1062297,"title":"","content":"I'd be happy to play CtL or WtF! Preferably 2e for the latter, and for the former... &quot;as 2e as possible&quot; is what I'd call it, i.e. using the CofD 2e base and maybe the &quot;any kith, any seeming&quot; deal. I'm fine with 1e Courts as well.<br /> <br /> I'm rabid to play some Changle, and 2e Woof got me interested to Woof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:23:33-07:00","id":1062331,"title":"","content":"Well, and here I was planning to run a 2ed-ish Changeling myself. MatabiMitsu,if you'd rather be a player than a ST, then consider yourself invited. Beans and everyone else (I think I can accomodate up to 5 people) is welcome too, of course. I find that modern settings are easier to handle, but if the demand for Dark Eras is high I could work with that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, any serious recruitment and team-building talk won't start until Monday 19th, but if you're fine with that I think we could work together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:42:25-07:00","id":1062338,"title":"","content":"Yes! 110% interested! Modern sounds great and Monday will give me time to actually buy and read the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13120-matatabimitsu","name":"MatatabiMitsu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:51:03-07:00","id":1062346,"title":"","content":"I was gifted... nearly all the 1e Changle pdfs, so I can share stuff from the supplements and/or tell you what's where (though the White Wolf Wiki can do that) if you don't want to buy everything right away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:54:21-07:00","id":1062350,"title":"","content":"Actually there just happens to be a Bundle of Holding sale of the whole set for scary cheap right now so I was just going to grab that and the 2e core book. Thanks for the offer though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13120-matatabimitsu","name":"MatatabiMitsu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T14:02:52-07:00","id":1062469,"title":"","content":"I have never played 2e or 1e for that matter, never played the old world changeling so I wouldn't even know where to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T16:14:06-07:00","id":1062531,"title":"","content":"If you have the 1e corebook (or at least the Quickstart rules) and are willing to give it a try, you're most welcome in the future game. A general read of the first chapter with the Lexicon is enough for a start, and any more specific lore details can be explained on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 03-14-2017, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T16:20:19-07:00","id":1062536,"title":"","content":"Are you likely to use the 1e Courts, or do you prefer the idea of 2e-esque making up our own Courts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T17:48:30-07:00","id":1062567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woland</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1062287-newbie-looking-to-join-run-pbp-game?p=1062531#post1062531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have the 1e corebook (or at least the Quickstart rules) and are willing to give it a try, you're most welcome in the future game. A general read of the first chapter with the Lexicon is enough for a start, and any more specific lore details can be explained on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have the 1e books just never played. But I will look for a future game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:03:52-07:00","id":1062570,"title":"","content":"Having glanced through a lot of 1e and 2e stuff today I really want to play a 2e Darkling. I think I even have a cool character concept brewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13120-matatabimitsu","name":"MatatabiMitsu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:08:16-07:00","id":1062572,"title":"","content":"I'd like to play changling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:09:32-07:00","id":1062574,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a Beast Fireheart &quot;hellhound&quot;, and if we go with Seasonal Courts, Autumn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:13:48-07:00","id":1062578,"title":"","content":"I was thinking Autumn too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13120-matatabimitsu","name":"MatatabiMitsu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:24:48-07:00","id":1062582,"title":"","content":"I have looked for Changeling the Los 2e on RPG DriveThru and i don't find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:33:48-07:00","id":1062585,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> - nope, Seasonal Courts are still a thing, at least in Europe (where the game will take place)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> - Changeling 2ed has not been released yet,although some materials have been published on Onyx Path's website. Mechanics-wise we will use the CofD rules + 1ed Changeling unless the latter was amended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:35:36-07:00","id":1062586,"title":"","content":"It is not yet released, sadly.<br /> However, a good deal of 2e Changeling material is already out there thanks to the Open Development, like the new Seeming/Kith system. That, and the 2e Chronicles of Darkness core, should be enough to allow us to cobble together a decently 2e-ish game.<br /> <br /> Edit: What Woland said.<br /> <br /> Also, yay! I honestly am pretty fond of the Seasonal Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T16:17:08-07:00","id":1063015,"title":"","content":"Well I decided since this will be my first character I wanted to avoid fixating on any single idea and ignoring other possibilities. So I used Random.org to roll 6 sets of 1-84 (kith) &amp; 1-6 (seeming), to give me a good random spread of concepts. That way I can look at all kinds of different angles and ideas. I'm going to come up with a simple character set-up for each of the combinations, and I might even go so far as to stat them all out just for practice. Then when the game rolls around I can figure out which of them I'd like to use.<br /> <br /> Oddly, I'm pretty sure fate wants me to play a Darkling since 3 of the 6 combinations I rolled came up Darkling. The 6 were: <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Soldier Darkling (with the 2e Darkling focus on loyalty this seems straightforward)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Waterborn Darkling (okay, I can work with this)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Render Fairest (huh, interesting)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Smith Darkling (I'm afraid to ask what they forged...)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Blightbent Elemental (ooo nuclear sludge elemental)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Chatelaine Elemental (I'm thinking an elemental of dusty stone or maybe ice)<br /> <br /> These all seem fun. I'm going to fiddle with them over the weekend and get used to character making. I'm really loving how free 2e is with pairing up seemings and kiths, I think it really opens things up.</b></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13120-matatabimitsu","name":"MatatabiMitsu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T17:04:44-07:00","id":1063030,"title":"","content":"It's great and really allows for fun things. For my Fireheart Beast hellhound lady, I'm thinking she had a background in law and an amateur interest in folklore, making her both a savvy creature of Court politics and an avid scholar of fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T06:36:04-07:00","id":1063198,"title":"","con